%S A076435 1,2,2,4,3,6,2,6,5,8,2,10,3,6,8,14,3,10,2,10,8,6,2,14,21,26,8,18,43,
%T A076435 14,2,10,6,6,7714,65476
%N A076435 Number of strongly regular simple graphs on n nodes.
%C A076435 The values through a(36) are obtained from the complete enumerations of strongly regular graphs summarized in Brouwer's tables. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 10 2026
%H A076435 A. E. Brouwer, <a href="https://aeb.win.tue.nl/graphs/srg/srgtab1-50.html">Strongly regular graphs on at most 50 vertices</a>.
%H A076435 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/StronglyRegularGraph.html">Strongly Regular Graph</a>
%F A076435 a(n) = A088741(n) + A000005(n) - 1, since the disconnected strongly regular graphs are the disjoint unions of equal-sized complete graphs, one for each proper divisor of n. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 10 2026
%e A076435 1: K_1 (1 graph)
%e A076435 2: \bar K_2, P_2 = K_2 (2 graph)
%e A076435 3: \bar K_3, C_3 = K_3 (2 graphs)
%e A076435 4: \bar K_4, 2P_2, C_4, K_4 (4 graphs)
%e A076435 5: C_5, \bar K_5, K_5 (3 graphs)
%e A076435 6: 2C_3, K_6, \bar K_6, 3P_2, Ci_6(1,2), K_{3,3} (6 graphs)
%e A076435 Here, \bar denotes the graph complement and Ci_n(...) a circular graph.
%Y A076435 Cf. A005176, A076434, A088741.
%K A076435 nonn,nice,more,changed
